# React Rules

## Component Structure
- Use functional components
- Components should follow Single Responsibility Principle
- Define prop types
- Keep component size appropriate

## State Management
- Use useState for simple state
- Use useReducer for complex state
- Use Context API or state management library for global state
- Prevent unnecessary state updates

## Hooks
- Use 'use' prefix for custom hooks
- Follow hook rules:
  - Only call hooks at the top level
  - Only call hooks from React functions
- Specify dependency arrays correctly
- Prevent unnecessary re-renders

## Performance
- Use React.memo appropriately
- Utilize useMemo and useCallback
- Prevent unnecessary re-renders
- Implement code splitting

## Props
- Minimize props drilling
- Use defaultProps
- Use prop-types or TypeScript
- Prevent unnecessary props passing
